{
  "email": "aisha.khan@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports Outlook inbox rules no longer sorting mail since last week. Checking account, devices, and mailbox usage per triage steps."
}

{
  "query": "Outlook inbox rules not moving mail to folders",
  "reason": "None of the provided articles cover Outlook inbox rules; searching for a matching how-to article."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0105",
  "reason": "Confirm the user's laptop is online and check for warnings that could affect Outlook rule processing."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thanks for reporting this. I checked your mailbox and your laptop, and both look healthy: your mailbox has plenty of free space and the laptop is online with no warnings. None of our standard guides cover inbox rules that stopped working, so I've passed your ticket to our second-level support team. They'll look into why your rules stopped sorting mail and will be in touch. In the meantime, please don't change or recreate your rules, since that may make it harder for them to see what happened.",
  "internal_note": "User aisha.khan (user_id 5, HR Generalist, America/New_York, usual hours 09:00-17:00). Account active, not blocked, no failed logins, password set 2026-09-11. Mailbox 12,500 of 51,200 MB used (24.4%), so KB-010 does not apply. Device BL-LT-0105 (Win 11 Pro) is online, last check-in 2026-10-11 02:48 UTC, 46.9% disk free, no warnings, so KB-009 does not apply (no sync symptoms reported). KB search returned no article on inbox rules. Rules are not moving mail since last week, and the cause is unknown. Not attempted: rule recreation, profile rebuild, or Outlook web comparison, since the ticket didn't say whether mail arrives in OWA. Suggested Tier 2 checks: whether the rules are still listed and enabled in Outlook and OWA, whether the server-side rule set is in error (for example, a rule referencing a deleted or renamed folder), whether a recent client or policy change affected rules, and whether the rules are being processed as client-side rules that did not survive a profile or client update. No actions were queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-009",
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
